WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.801
-Hi!
-Hi, bud.

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.100
-Hello!
-Stunning, as always.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.834
Thank you for coming back
on our show.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.100
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.100
-Do you remember the last time
we saw each other?

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.167
-I do. Do you remember?

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.868
-Do you remember?
-But do you remember?

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:13.901
-We were dancing.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:16.300
-We were dancing to
Justin Bieber.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.567
-We saw "Biebs."
-We saw The Biebs.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:21.100
-Yeah, we're "Beliebers." And --
-Big-time.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.033
-We were at the Met Gala.
-Yes.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:24.467
-And Justin Bieber
came out and performed.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:25.601
He was awesome.
-Yeah.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:26.968
-And I saw you.
-He had a ski mask on.

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:28.067
-He did.
-He did.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.801
-Wear a mask, everybody.
-Yes, wear a mask.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.267
-A ski mask.
But whatever. It's close enough.

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.067
But we were there,
and I saw you and I go,

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.234
"Oh, my God, I have to go over
to Julia and start dancing."

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.767
-I was very excited.
I was just like, "Oh, my God."

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:42.033
-Both of us!
-Yeah, we were just like --

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:44.067
-And we were rocking out.
It was so much fun.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.968
-We were like --
-Oh, yeah, we were so excited.

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:48.400
I'm like, "This is a memory."
We created a memory.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.133
Because you know
I'm a giant fan.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.167
I go, "I know and --"
I'm caught up.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.234
I'm caught up.
No spoilers, but I'm caught up.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.901
Not completely caught up,

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.734
but I'm more recent
than I was last time.

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:59.834
-Listen, Jimmy,
you're a busy guy.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.934
You have this every night.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.100
-You know, you have a family.
-Yeah, thank you.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.667
-Yeah, I get it.
-Thank you so much. Yeah.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.100
No, but I wanted --
-Give it up for Jimmy!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.133
-No, no, no.
That's not what I --

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.300
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.133
No, that's not my point.
That's not what I wanted.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:14.968
My point was, it's so good,
and you were so good.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.534
And everyone in the whole
cast -- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:18.934
But you --
Everyone I tell "Ozark" --

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.234
I go, "Have you seen 'Ozark'?"

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.267
If they haven't seen it, I go,
"Watch the first episode

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.267
and then call me the next day

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:26.100
and tell me who
Julia Garner is."

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.167
And they're like -- Dude,
you just crush it every episode.

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.300
You're so good.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.501
-Thank you so much.
That means a lot.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.601
-I know, sorry, yeah.
-No. Are you kidding?

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:35.200
Like, I'm really trying to play
it cool right now,

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.667
but I'm actually,
like, terrified.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.734
-Well, there's this scene that
people are talking about online.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.033
I tried not to look at it,

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.467
because I don't want
any spoilers.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:47.901
But, apparently,
you scream in --

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:50.934
-Yes. Which that can be, like,
any scene in "Ozark."

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:52.467
I mean, it's not -- But no.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.601
But this is not
a typical scream. No.

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:58.234
-No, it's not.
-I'm mad.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.434
-You really are.
-I'm very, very angry.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.667
-You're really angry.
-I'm very angry.

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:05.634
-Can we show the video of
the scream at least?

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.300
-If you want to stop me,

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.667
you're going to have to
[bleep] kill me!

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:22.567
-How in the --
How do you do this?

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:24.200
-I was hungry. No, I'm kidding.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.133
-But you are not that person.
This is acting.

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:30.667
-That's acting.
-It is acting.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.701
-I am an actor.
-Yes!

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:34.367
-I look very angry there.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:37.133
-You are mad!
-Mad!

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:39.300
-The picture --
I can't even hold it.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.968
It shakes.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.834
-Ugh! Jason Bateman!

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.634
-I go,
what inspires you for that?

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:48.667
And very interesting answer.
It's art.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.968
-Yes. So, I'm very visual
and I get inspired from

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:56.968
different things, and I really
kind of just wanted

00:02:56.968 --> 00:03:00.434
the spirit of, like,
a Caravaggio painting

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:01.634
and the darkness.

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.834
And, you know,
I feel like Caravaggio paints

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.167
intensity and chaos so well.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.901
So I -- Yes. Yeah.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.100
-I love their
ice-cream cakes, too.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.601
Caravaggio.
-Yes, yes.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.767
And their gelatos, right?

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:15.067
-But your dad is --
-Yes, he's an art teacher.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:16.100
Yes, an artist, yeah.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.501
-So you know all about this.
-Yeah.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:18.601
-This is one of the paintings

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:19.667
that inspired you
for the scream.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:20.868
-Well, I like the chaos.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:22.534
And, you know, she's obviously

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:23.968
getting, you know, defensive.

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:25.267
I mean, she has snakes as hair.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.067
-Yeah, she's lost her head.
-Yes, she's very mad.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:30.067
Yes, yes. She's very -- Yes.
-Angry. That's one.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:33.501
-Yes. And then, yeah,
that's another one.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.868
But, this is not --
You know, not the faces.

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:38.100
I just like the chaos of it.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.868
I kind of just wanted my mind to

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:42.300
feel kind of claustrophobic
like that.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.200
-And so you get into the zone.
You look at these.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.400
-But that wasn't really doing --
So, I got inspired by it,

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.734
but there was
still something missing.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:54.634
And then I realized Mike Tyson

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.801
is also another
inspiration for me.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:04:01.601
And I really got inspired from
this photo, as well.

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:02.868
-Yeah.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.000
-I --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.067
-That was --
-So -- But here's the thing.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:12.000
Mike Tyson -- this face could be
in a Caravaggio painting.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.334
I mean, don't you think so?

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:14.968
-Yes, it could be a Caravaggio.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:17.534
-Yes, a character from
a Caravaggio painting.

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:21.934
So I really got inspired from,
you know, that spirit.

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:24.968
-This was the Holyfield fight.
-Yes.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.400
-Yeah.
-He was very mad there, too.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.868
-You think?

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.634
I want to talk about
your new show, "Inventing Anna."

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:34.934
By the way, it premieres --
Netflix, February 11th.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:37.100
It's based on a true story,
a really cool story.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:40.334
-Yes, it's based off
a Cut article.

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:47.033
And it's about this girl who
scams New York's high society

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.767
and pretends to be something
that she's not.

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:52.067
I don't really know --
She's a very complex character.

00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:53.767
It's kind of better to watch it.

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:56.901
-I remember reading about her in
the "New York Post" and stuff

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.000
and like, "Wait, what happened?

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.234
How did she do this?"

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.000
-She's a New York poster child,
I feel like, yes.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.467
-She was.
-Yes.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:06.667
-And, again, a great accent,
a great voice you do with that.

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:09.334
-That was probably the
hardest accent I've ever done.

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:11.868
It was a different mixture
of accents.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:17.133
So, you know,
this is a girl who is saying

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.067
that she's German,
but she's really Russian,

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.567
so she's not going to have
a Russian accent.

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:24.300
[ German accent ] So, first,
I had to do, like, a European --

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.567
like, a German accent, right?

00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:26.968
But, you know, it's very subtle.

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:28.367
It's like, you know, have
a vocal fry at the end of it.

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:29.801
Whatever, right?

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:35.267
[ Russian accent ] And then,
you know, I had to add, like,

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.434
some little Russian
for certain words.

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:39.267
It was a very bad
Russian accent.

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:41.868
But then I start to do, like --

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.701
This is more of an
Anna Delvey accent.

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:46.734
And then it gets Americanized,
because you know how Americans

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:49.200
kind of add the question
at the end of everything?

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.968
Like, you know what I mean?

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:54.033
Like, Europeans
don't do that, right?

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:56.367
-Come on. What just happened?

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.000
Yo, that was --

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:03.767
That will go in the history
books of how to act right there.

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.834
In 10 seconds,
you just did something --

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:07.434
Everyone's face
is melted right now.

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:08.667
Everyone's like, "What?!"

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:11.000
-So, really, my --
I really wanted to make sure

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.434
that it was kind of one
of those things,

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:13.934
if she goes back to Europe,

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:16.868
all of her European friends are
like, "You sound so American."

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:18.133
And then all of her friends
here are like,

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:20.801
"Oh, my God,
you sound so European."

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:23.734
-Yeah, exactly.
-Like, OMG. Oh, my God, Anna.

00:06:23.734 --> 00:06:26.868
-I know.
-I really like your, like --

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:28.934
-You do? Thank you.

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:32.434
Did you do it for her?
-Yes.

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:35.868
So, I went to go
visit her in jail, and --

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:39.067
-♪ Spoiler alert! ♪

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:44.033
-So, I went to visit her,
and she was like,

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:48.400
"So, uh --
So, how's the shoot going?"

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.067
And I said,
"Oh, it's going well."

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:52.567
And, you know,
I'm super-intimidated.

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:54.300
Like, she's Anna Delvey.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:59.000
And she's like,
"So, um, how you playing me?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.167
How you playing me?"

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:02.300
And I said, "Uh, well..."

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:03.601
She's like,
"Like, what are you doing

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:05.634
with my character, you know?"

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:08.000
And I said --
I didn't know what to do,

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.100
so I started mirroring her.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:10.868
I was like,
"Well, how you playing me?

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:12.701
What you doing
with my character?"

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:14.033
And she was like --
[ Giggles ]

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.634
"That's so funny!"

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:16.667
And then I did.

00:07:16.667 --> 00:07:18.100
I was like, "Ah-ha!
That's so funny!"

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.868
And then the journalist
that wrote the article

00:07:19.868 --> 00:07:20.934
was sitting there.

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:23.334
It got really meta.
-Wow!

00:07:23.334 --> 00:07:24.801
-And she's fascinating.
I -- Yeah.

00:07:24.801 --> 00:07:25.968
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:28.000
Here's Julia Garner in
"Inventing Anna."

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.167
Take a look at this.

00:07:29.167 --> 00:07:32.334
-All men underestimate women.

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:34.601
Even the one
who's supposed to love us.

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:37.167
-Did Alan underestimate you?

00:07:37.167 --> 00:07:38.701
Is that why you humiliated him?

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:41.000
-You're so worried about Alan.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:45.400
Do you seriously think he's in
any danger of losing anything?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.601
I'm the one locked up
for crimes I didn't commit.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.267
I'm the one denied bail.

00:07:50.267 --> 00:07:53.133
Every day, men do far worse
things than anything

00:07:53.133 --> 00:07:55.801
I've allegedly done,
and what happens to them?

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:58.133
Nothing. No consequences,
no fallout,

00:07:58.133 --> 00:08:00.300
and definitely no jail time.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.367
Alan will be fine,

00:08:01.367 --> 00:08:03.100
and they'll
probably promote him.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.033
Men fail upwards all the time.

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:07.033
[ Buzz, cell door closes ]

00:08:07.033 --> 00:08:09.267
-Oh, that's how you do it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:11.267
Julia Garner, everyone!

00:08:11.267 --> 00:08:12.501
"Inventing Anna" premieres

00:08:12.501 --> 00:08:14.300
February 11th on Netflix.

